{"compatibility":"minor","safety_note_md":"# SafeStan Safety Note

Compatibility: minor.

Protected data: `y`.

Generated files: `model_safe.stan`, `data_safe.json`.

Changes: removed the unused parameter `beta`. It is not referenced in transformed parameters or in the model block and contributes no log-density term, but SafeStan requires every top-level parameter to have exactly one built-in prior sampling statement. The protected likelihood for `y` and the log density over all retained parameters are unchanged. The data file is unchanged.
","model_safe_stan":"data {
  int<lower=0> J;
  int<lower=0> N;
  array[N] int<lower=1, upper=J> county;
  vector[J] u;
  vector[N] x;
  vector[N] y;
}
parameters {
  vector[J] a;
  real b;
  real g_0;
  real g_1;
  real<lower=0, upper=100> sigma_a;
  real<lower=0, upper=100> sigma_y;
}
transformed parameters {
  vector[J] a_hat;
  vector[J] e_a;
  vector[N] y_hat;

  for (j in 1 : J) {
    a_hat[j] = 100 * g_0 + 100 * g_1 * u[j];
  }
  e_a = a - a_hat;

  for (i in 1 : N) {
    y_hat[i] = a[county[i]] + x[i] * b * 100;
  }
}
model {
  g_0 ~ normal(0, 1);
  g_1 ~ normal(0, 1);

  sigma_a ~ uniform(0, 100);
  a ~ normal(a_hat, sigma_a);

  b ~ normal(0, 1);

  sigma_y ~ uniform(0, 100);
  y ~ normal(y_hat, sigma_y);
}
","data_safe_json":"{"J":2,"N":1,"county":[1],"u":[6.757387877791891,4.9849101738584825],"x":[3.0228357993572157],"y":[1.0]}","protected_variables":["y"]}
